.Dd November 10, 2026
.Dt QEMU-VMSR-HELPER 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm qemu-vmsr-helper
.Nd read RAPL energy counters for QEMU's virtual RAPL MSRs
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl d
.Op Fl f Ar pidfile
.Op Fl k Ar socket
.Op Fl T Ar trace
.Op Fl u Ar user
.Op Fl g Ar group
.Nm
.Fl h | V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is Debian's QEMU helper that reads a processor package's RAPL energy
counters from
.Pa /dev/cpu/N/msr
on behalf of a QEMU that runs with
.Ql -accel kvm,rapl=true,rapl-helper-socket= Ns Ar socket ,
which may not read them itself.
It answers QEMU on the Unix socket
.Ar socket ,
which must be the one QEMU names.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl d , Fl -daemon
Run in the background.
.It Fl f , Fl -pidfile Ns = Ns Ar pidfile
Write the process ID to
.Ar pidfile
when running in the background; the default is
.Pa /var/run/qemu-vmsr-helper.pid .
.It Fl k , Fl -socket Ns = Ns Ar socket
Listen on
.Ar socket ;
the default is
.Pa /var/run/qemu-vmsr-helper.sock .
.It Fl T , Fl -trace Ar trace
Turn on QEMU's trace events, as
.Xr qemu-system 1
describes.
.It Fl u , Fl -user Ns = Ns Ar user
.It Fl g , Fl -group Ns = Ns Ar group
Drop privileges to
.Ar user
and
.Ar group
once the socket is open.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the options and exit.
.It Fl V , Fl -version
Print the version and exit.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr qemu-system 1 ,
.Xr qemu-pr-helper 8
.Sh RACH2
Debian ships no page for this program; this one is written from QEMU's
source and its RAPL document.
The helper checks for an Intel processor and for
.Pa /sys/class/powercap/intel-rapl/enabled
before it reads its options, and exits with
.Dq CPU is not INTEL cpu
or
.Dq RAPL driver not enable
where either is missing, as on Rach2, which has no RAPL driver.
The package's copyright and license terms are installed under
.Pa /usr/share/doc/qemu-system-common/copyright .
